<title>MEXICO: Mexico's top corn growing state sees good '96 crop.</title>
<headline>Mexico's top corn growing state sees good '96 crop.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jalisco, Mexico's top corn growing state, will harvest 2,263,564 tonnes of white corn this year, an official of the state office of the Agriculture Ministry forecast Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is expected that 2,263,564 tonnes will be harvested against the 2,100,000 tonnes produced last year,&quot; Jorge Martinez, an official with the ministry's market information service, said in an interview here in the state capital.</p>
<p>Martinez said the state had registered 701,622 hectares planted to the end of August, with reports of 3,630 hectares of corn plantings damaged by adverse weather.</p>
<p>In 1995, Jalisco produced 15.3 percent of the country's corn harvest.</p>
<p>--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau (523) 817-0397</p>
</text>
